`:PROCEDURE Name(...)` with the keyword form but a parameter list: SSL
procedures take arguments through :PARAMETERS. procedure_declaration_syntax
fires on the `(` (parenthesized-parameters path). The block still opens
and pairs with :ENDPROC (diag.procedure_declaration_syntax).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CalcShipping(nWeight, sZone);
	:DECLARE nCost;
	nCost := nWeight * 1.5;
	:RETURN nCost;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CalcShipping(nWeight, sZone);
	:DECLARE nCost;

	nCost := nWeight * 1.5;

	:RETURN nCost;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:24-1:25 error procedure_declaration_syntax: Procedure declarations don't take parentheses. Use ":PROCEDURE Name;" and declare arguments via ":PARAMETERS".
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:24-1:25 error procedure_declaration_syntax: Procedure declarations don't take parentheses. Use ":PROCEDURE Name;" and declare arguments via ":PARAMETERS".
3:11-3:18 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'nWeight' is not declared
